templates/table.html              table browser
templates/row_view.html           single-row editor
templates/api_playground.html     API recipes
templates/docs.html               OpenAPI viewer
templates/schema_docs.html        rendered schema documentation
templates/query_syntax.html       rendered query contract documentation
doc/schema_manager_guide.md       Markdown Schema Manager and XML schema documentation
doc/dynamic_api_query_syntax.md   Markdown query contract documentation
static/dynamic_api.css            shared UI styles
static/demo_schema.xml             browser-loadable copy of the bundled demo schema
static/schema_manager_guide.md     browser-loadable Markdown schema guide
static/schema_app.xsd              browser-loadable raw schema XSD
schema/schema_app.xsd              local XSD used by deployed Schema Manager validation
static/dynamic_api_browser.js     query/table/row/docs/playground behavior
static/schema_manager.js          Schema Manager behavior
```


## Bundled demo schema

The generated app starts with a ready-to-apply schema in two places:

```text
schema/app.schema.xml
static/demo_schema.xml
```

It creates four tables for the first run:

```text
categories
customers
products
orders
```

Use `/schema-manager` -> `Load demo schema` to load it into the editor. `Build plan` is a preview step. `Apply live plan` changes the configured SQLite database path unless `Only dry-run` is checked.


## Showcase pages

- `/query-builder` includes a SQL-to-payload Query Builder, structured WHERE, raw filter strings, JOIN, GROUP BY, HAVING, ORDER BY, LIMIT and write payload examples.
- `/api-playground` presents beginner-friendly recipes in a two-column layout: choose a recipe on the left and inspect request/response on the right.
- The generated app enables `allowRawJoin` for the showcase so users can test JOIN examples immediately.


### One-click demo setup

The generated app exposes `POST /api/demo/setup`. It resets only the generated app SQLite database, writes the bundled demo schema, creates `categories`, `customers`, `products`, `orders`, and seeds rows used by `/query-builder`, `/table`, and `/api-playground`.



## Schema documentation

The generated app includes a text guide for the Schema Manager workflow and XML schema contract:

```text
GET /docs/schema
doc/schema_manager_guide.md
static/schema_manager_guide.md
static/schema_app.xsd
```

Use it as the onboarding reference for editing `schema/app.schema.xml`, understanding `Application`, `Configuration`, `DataStructure`, `Entity`, `Field`, `ForeignKeyField`, `Index`, validation errors, diff output, plan output, apply confirmations and schema history.

## Query syntax documentation

The generated app includes a text specification for the current Dynamic API query contract:

```text
GET /docs/query-syntax
doc/dynamic_api_query_syntax.md
```

Use it as the authoritative onboarding reference for JSON envelopes sent to `POST /api/dynamic`, table-specific CRUD shortcuts, metadata endpoints, structured `where`, raw `filter`, `join`, `group_by`, `having`, sorting and limits.
